# A male's appetite lights
# The three lights on a male that show how hungry he is: an orange level light (his O
# appetite), a greenish level light (his P appetite), and the white ring above his head,
# which follows whichever of the two is the stronger. His blinking head ring is a
# different thing - see male-calling.
# Watch one male from switch-on and you should see exactly this.

0 The three lights are switched on, but at zero brightness. You still see nothing on him.
-> one-appetite-rising : O appetite, orange light
-> one-appetite-rising : P appetite, greenish light
2.4 Two and a half seconds later the lights show their first real value: each level light lit in proportion to its own appetite, the white ring above his head in proportion to the stronger of the two. Both males start around a tenth full, so this is very dim - a faint glow, not an obvious light.
237 They then brighten one small step every 2.4 seconds, continuously, for the next four minutes, until both level lights and the ring are at full brightness.
0 They never dim again by themselves. A male who has been running for more than four minutes is simply fully lit and stays so. If you see one dim down, somebody reset him from the control page.
